{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1119085-caerns-with-religious-significance","id":1119085,"title":"Caerns with religious significance","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Werewolf: The Apocalypse"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-07-21T15:14:25-07:00","id":1119085,"title":"Caerns with religious significance","content":"So, I'm in the process of prepping a Roll20 WtA game set in Tucson. I'd like to place a Caern somewhere in one of the old neighborhoods in the city, and thought that I had found the perfect place. Then I started to talk myself out of it. Basically El Tiradito is a nominally Catholic shrine in the Barrio Viejo neighborhood in Tucson. I say nominally because its not owned or officially endorsed by the Catholic church or any church. The story goes that, many years ago, a jealous husband murdered his wife's true love and buried him right in front of the house. The shrine is supposed to be the location where he was buried. People often come there to light candles leave and leave little pieces of paper in the crevices of the wall with prayers or wishes on them. In fact, the place has come to be known as &quot;The Wishing Shrine.&quot; So the place has a quasi Christian significance, but it has the quasi-heretical folk Christian vibe that is common to Mexico. So I guess my question is, do you think a place like that could become a Caern? I mean, look, I get that its MY game and I can do whatever I want. But are there examples in the WoD of places with religious significance becoming Caerns, or would the Christian symbolism leave a bad taste in the spirits' mouths?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1702-matty1love","name":"Matty1Love","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"43"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-21T15:17:06-07:00","id":1119087,"title":"","content":"Well, in W:TA it's all about the Garou blessing the location. There's plenty of nodes that are churches in Mages so I don't see a problem here. I'd be inclined to make it a Child of Gaia sanctuary and have them subtly shift the veneration of the Virgin to Gaia but that's just me.<br /> <br /> I've had a couple of Churches and Christian holy places actually be Garou sanctuaries in my game.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-21T16:11:08-07:00","id":1119100,"title":"","content":"Well, I wrote this, hope it offers some inspiration.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong> Sept of Luna's Eternal Vigil</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Location: Scotland.<br /> <br /> <br /> Location description: An ancient and powerful sept, Luna's Eternal Vigil or just Vigil, is a place of learning for the Silver Fangs. It is also a place where the metis of the tribe are sent to be kept, safely away from the eyes of the Nation. As the sept is technically a monastery, it is split between males and females. Contact with the other sex is often minimal, though Ragabash are known to sneak around. The Vigil is a large place built into the mountain itself, though there are a lot of minor buildings used to support the sept. It has large gardens, classrooms for students. And one of the most expansive libraries of garou literature in the Nation. The Sept also houses its share of kinfolk monks and nuns, whether from those who'd rather worship than breed, to those who are taken there to be safe from the dangers of their home septs.<br /> <br /> As Vigil has tended metis since the days of Dark Ages, they have a veritable wealth of knowledge on the middle breed and how to deal with rowdy cubs. The metis in turn receive a decent education, and are treated well. However, each is named in latin either after their deformities, or by auspice. This name mimics the renaming of monks of ancient times, and implies the metis are not to leave the Sept. There are wards and guards for those who still try.</div> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-21T16:18:54-07:00","id":1119102,"title":"","content":"Is there a conflict between the Gaian energy there and any True Faith? If there is, then there would be trouble because True Faith has an effect on the Gauntlet and Rage. However, absent True Faith issues I don't think there'd be a concern. El Tiradito falls more into the folk belief category than actual Christian belief. It's like people burying statues of St. Joseph to help sell their home. The Church is emphatic that this is wrong - it is superstition, not faith. But some people do it anyway. In choosing the caern's purpose though, you'd want to select one that doesn't clash with the folk Cathiolicism beliefs of the area though, but complement it.<br /> <br /> I do hope that your setting has some more caerns than just an urban one in Tucson. There are some really interesting places out there. The Madrean Sky Islands are a perfect place for a wilderness caern, and the Sonoran Desert is the greenest/wettest desert in the world. Arizona is really a diverse place with desert, pine forests, deciduous forests, wetlands, grasslands, and chaparral (even tundra up by Flagstaff). The White Mountain and San Carlos Apache Indian reservations are not too far, and next to them is the US Fish &amp; Wildlife Service program to reintroduce the Mexican Wolf subspecies. The Garou protectorates likely includes both sides of the border. It can be a very cool setting for a chronicle.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-21T16:40:54-07:00","id":1119112,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Black Fox</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1119085-caerns-with-religious-significance?p=1119102#post1119102\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is there a conflict between the Gaian energy there and any True Faith? If there is, then there would be trouble because True Faith has an effect on the Gauntlet and Rage. However, absent True Faith issues I don't think there'd be a concern. El Tiradito falls more into the folk belief category than actual Christian belief. It's like people burying statues of St. Joseph to help sell their home. The Church is emphatic that this is wrong - it is superstition, not faith. But some people do it anyway. In choosing the caern's purpose though, you'd want to select one that doesn't clash with the folk Cathiolicism beliefs of the area though, but complement it.<br /> <br /> I do hope that your setting has some more caerns than just an urban one in Tucson. There are some really interesting places out there. The Madrean Sky Islands are a perfect place for a wilderness caern, and the Sonoran Desert is the greenest/wettest desert in the world. Arizona is really a diverse place with desert, pine forests, deciduous forests, wetlands, grasslands, and chaparral (even tundra up by Flagstaff). The White Mountain and San Carlos Apache Indian reservations are not too far, and next to them is the US Fish &amp; Wildlife Service program to reintroduce the Mexican Wolf subspecies. The Garou protectorates likely includes both sides of the border. It can be a very cool setting for a chronicle.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah definitely wasn't planning on El Tiradito having a True Faith rating. And I totally agree that the American southwest (and Arizona, in particular) is chock full of beautiful wilderness and plenty of good places for caerns. That said, I do have to limit my scope, somewhat, as I want the chronicle to have a local feel. Other than El Tiradito (which is going to be a Bone Gnawer caern), there will be another caern west of Tucson in the Rincon Mountain District of Saguaro National Park. That one is going to be a mixed tribal Sept. Both caerns will be relatively small. El Tiradito will be a level 1 Caern and the other, 1 or 2. I will probably make mention of a number of other caerns in the general vicinity without actually statting out every NPC that populates those septs. But that nearby USFW program to reintroduce Mexican wolves was part of the reason I chose this area for the setting.<br /> <br /> As for what type of caern, I'm leaning towards a caern of Gnosis for El Tiradito. The other I'm still in the process of fleshing it out.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1702-matty1love","name":"Matty1Love","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"43"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-22T10:21:44-07:00","id":1119275,"title":"","content":"Given the backstory of the area I think I would lean more towards a caern of vengeance or justice. Caerns of gnosis tend to be rare and very rarely in the hands of Bone Gnawers.<br /> \u200b","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/293-lncbill","name":"lncbill","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar293_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-24T07:44:42-07:00","id":1119870,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lncbill</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1119085-caerns-with-religious-significance?p=1119275#post1119275\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Given the backstory of the area I think I would lean more towards a caern of vengeance or justice. Caerns of gnosis tend to be rare and very rarely in the hands of Bone Gnawers.<br /> \u200b</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Eh I don't see vengeance or justice. If you were going just by the legend of how the place came to be, then yeah, I guess. But the reason why people keep coming there is to pray and make wishes, which garners a resonance of peace and hopefulness, IMO. Maybe Willpower?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6039-mattlutz","name":"MattLutz","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-27T11:18:32-07:00","id":1121416,"title":"","content":"The reason people visit the shrine seems to be for healing of their own hearts after being heartbroken. The entire legend is one of tragedy after all, not only is Juan killed, but the entire family is taken out in short order. I think the caern's purpose is best suited being built on that. It would be like a Caern of Healing, but more like Emotional Healing instead of physical healing. So I guess a Caern of Empathy is the best description. &quot;Comfort&quot; or &quot;Succor&quot; would be another appropriate term.<br /> <br /> Most Garou would not be interested in such a caern, so it falling to the Bone Gnawers would make sense. Only the Children of Gaia would be the only other tribe interested in it with the Uktena having an intellectual interest.<br /> <br /> People who have been betrayed, falling into Harano, in severe grief, or some other kind of Depression go there to become healed and renew their purpose in life. So regaining Willpower in certain kind of circumstances would be appropriate, but not all kinds. Suppression or removal of certain Derangements might also happen. I could also see, in certain circumstances Gnosis gained, or (to a lesser extent) even Rage might be recovered, but only in cases where grief and sorrow might have limited them beforehand.<br /> <br /> Activating the Caern might lead to bonuses in Empathy or Enigmas.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-27T16:59:33-07:00","id":1121621,"title":"","content":"I agree with the last couple of posts: the caern's power should be related to the energy associated with it at present. A challenge for any garou trying to occupy and use the caern would be how to deal with the human pilgrims who are approaching it all the time.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13713-wilson","name":"Wilson","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"182"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-30T04:33:10-07:00","id":1122666,"title":"","content":"The religious aspect I'd say is the least problematic. The issue I'd see for the sept would be maintaining the Veil since the location is generally accessable to the public. How do you hide doing moots?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-31T20:07:02-07:00","id":1123285,"title":"","content":"Sept of the Wheel of Ptah (Page 96 Caerns: Places of Power) is located in the Mosque of Anfa in Casablanca. The Firebird Sept (set in the possibly fictitious Russian city of Zagorsk) is also located in a Russian Orthodox church.<br /> <br /> \u200bEDIT: Now that I think about it, there was also a Child of Gaia sept somewhere in rural Spain that was also located in a working (albeit obscure) Catholic monastery.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/19/w20supporterheavymetal1.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/546/wpur.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/545/7z8m.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/829/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":3506,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3506-uniform-two-six","user":"Uniform Two Six","date":". 07-31-2017, 11:09 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3506-uniform-two-six","name":"Uniform Two Six","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3506_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"455"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-31T22:28:22-07:00","id":1123318,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Uniform Two Six</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1119085-caerns-with-religious-significance?p=1123285#post1123285\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sept of the Wheel of Ptah (Page 96 Caerns: Places of Power) is located in the Mosque of Anfa in Casablanca. The Firebird Sept (set in the possibly fictitious Russian city of Zagorsk) is also located in a Russian Orthodox church.<br /> \u200bEDIT: Now that I think about it, there was also a Child of Gaia sept somewhere in rural Spain that was also located in a working (albeit obscure) Catholic monastery.</div> </div> </div> </div>Generally Churches have all sorts of areas you can't just walk into whether its the private rooms of the clergy there, special shrines etc. Most of the ones described sound like fairly large multibuilding complexes(especially the monestary)<br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/El_Tiradito\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/ac/El_Tiradito_shrine_%28Tucson%2C_Arizona%29_2.JPG/1280px-El_Tiradito_shrine_%28Tucson%2C_Arizona%29_2.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=index&amp;utm_content=thumbnail\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/El_Tiradito\" target=\"_blank\"> El Tiradito - Wikipedia </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/El_Tiradito\" target=\"_blank\"> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/El_Tiradito </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> It looks very small and very open. It seems more like what one of the more solitary breeds might tend.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-03T09:01:10-07:00","id":1124322,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Uniform Two Six</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1119085-caerns-with-religious-significance?p=1123285#post1123285\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sept of the Wheel of Ptah (Page 96 Caerns: Places of Power) is located in the Mosque of Anfa in Casablanca. The Firebird Sept (set in the possibly fictitious Russian city of Zagorsk) is also located in a Russian Orthodox church.<br /> <br /> \u200bEDIT: Now that I think about it, there was also a Child of Gaia sept somewhere in rural Spain that was also located in a working (albeit obscure) Catholic monastery.</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200bIf I remember that Caern actually became a Shadow Lord one it was in the Dark Ages book.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/293-lncbill","name":"lncbill","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar293_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-04T11:22:42-07:00","id":1124846,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1119085-caerns-with-religious-significance?p=1123318#post1123318\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Generally Churches have all sorts of areas you can't just walk into whether it's the private rooms of the clergy there, special shrines etc. Most of the ones described sound like fairly large multibuilding complexes (especially the monestary)<br /> ...<br /> It looks very small and very open. It seems more like what one of the more solitary breeds might tend.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, large, old buildings will have basements and catacombs, but in any case you'll either have to have an open agreement with the local clergy or BE the local clergy. I doubt ordinary priests are going to be okay with a sept of Gaia-worshipping werewolves living in their church, unless maybe the Garou interpret the Gaian spirit world through a Christian lens, which in my opinion would not be an easy sell.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13713-wilson","name":"Wilson","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"182"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}